  {
    "id": "convex",
    "label": "Convex reduced p99 query latency by over 50%",
    "theme": "customer-case convex",
    "html": "<div class=\"case-heading convex-heading\"><img class=\"convex-title-symbol\" src=\"assets/convex-symbol-color.svg\" alt=\"\"><h2>Convex reduced p99 query latency by over 50%</h2></div><div class=\"convex-curves\"><div class=\"convex-original-grid\"><div><div class=\"source-provider-row\"><span>AWS Aurora</span><span>PlanetScale Postgres</span></div><div class=\"convex-source-frame\"><img src=\"assets/convex-original-results.png\" alt=\"Original Convex index query latency chart. All five percentile curves, original axes and legend are preserved; values are in seconds.\"></div><div class=\"convex-result\"><span>Query p99</span><div>10–15 ms <i>→</i> <strong>5–7 ms</strong></div></div></div><div><div class=\"source-provider-row\"><span>AWS Aurora</span><span>PlanetScale Postgres</span></div><div class=\"convex-source-frame commit-source\"><img src=\"assets/convex-original-results.png\" alt=\"Original Convex database commit latency chart. All five percentile curves, original axes and legend are preserved; values are in seconds.\"></div><div class=\"convex-result\"><span>Batch-commit p99</span><div>75–200 ms <i>→</i> <strong>~20 ms</strong></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"convex-quote\"><q>p50 is the new p99.</q><span>Jamie Turner | CEO of Context</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "id": "depot",
    "label": "Depot: latency and historical analytics",
    "theme": "teach teach-depot",
    "html": "<h2>Depot: faster queries, <span class=\"accent\">more history.</span></h2>\n<p class=\"depot-scope\">Vitess / MySQL · PlanetScale EBS → Metal</p>\n<div class=\"depot-evidence\">\n  <figure class=\"depot-cpu-proof\">\n    <figcaption><span>EBS · 8 CPUs</span><span class=\"accent\">Metal · 4 CPUs</span></figcaption>\n    <img class=\"depot-cpu-image\" src=\"assets/depot-iowait-original.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"202\" alt=\"Original Depot CPU usage chart across January 22–28. The stacked chart includes iowait, irq, nice, softirq, steal, system and user CPU time. Depot reports I/O wait disappeared after moving from EBS-backed PS-400 with 8 CPUs to Metal M-320 with 4 CPUs. The source chart is preserved, including its axes and legend; no exact migration timestamp is added.\">\n    <div class=\"depot-insight fragment\" data-fragment-index=\"0\"><span class=\"insight-rule\"></span><span>I/O wait disappeared.</span></div>\n  </figure>\n  <div class=\"depot-percentiles\" aria-label=\"Depot customer-reported query latency\">\n    <div class=\"depot-percentile\"><p>p95 query latency</p><div class=\"percentile-values\"><span>40</span><span class=\"metric-arrow\">→</span><span class=\"accent\">5<span class=\"metric-unit\"> ms</span></span></div><div class=\"percentile-gain accent\">8× faster</div></div>\n    <div class=\"depot-percentile\"><p>p99 query latency</p><div class=\"percentile-values secondary\"><span>50</span><span class=\"metric-arrow\">→</span><span class=\"accent\">30<span class=\"metric-unit\"> ms</span></span></div></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"depot-history\" aria-label=\"Build analytics metadata retention changed from 7, 30 or 90 days by plan to removal of those plan limits; local physical storage still has finite capacity.\">\n <div class=\"history-copy\"><p class=\"retention-label\">Build analytics retention</p><div class=\"history-words\"><span class=\"fragment fade-out history-before\" data-fragment-index=\"1\">7 / 30 / 90-day limits</span><span class=\"fragment history-after accent\" data-fragment-index=\"1\">Retention limits removed.</span></div><p class=\"history-benefit fragment\" data-fragment-index=\"1\">More complete historical analytics.</p></div>\n <svg class=\"depot-history-art\" viewBox=\"0 0 570 128\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Schematic history timeline: plan retention boundary disappears and more historical records become available. Blocks are illustrative, not measured days or physical capacity.\">\n  <defs><pattern id=\"depot-history-dots\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" fill=\"#f35815\"/></pattern></defs>\n  <path d=\"M4 72H550\" stroke=\"#414141\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#202020\" stroke=\"#777\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"144\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/></g>\n  <g class=\"fragment fade-out\" data-fragment-index=\"1\"><path d=\"M222 17V111\" stroke=\"#ff4d4d\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><text x=\"235\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#a5a5a5\" font-family=\"ui-monospace,monospace\" font-size=\"18\">Retention limit</text></g>\n  <g class=\"fragment history-extension\" data-fragment-index=\"1\" fill=\"url(#depot-history-dots)\" stroke=\"#f35815\"><path d=\"M190 72H554\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"272\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"336\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"400\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/><rect x=\"464\" y=\"45\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\"/></g>\n </svg>\n</div>",
    "hidden": true
  },
  {
    "id": "fit",
    "label": "Metal tradeoffs: local I/O versus Aurora network storage",
    "theme": "teach teach-tradeoffs",
    "html": "<h2><span class=\"accent\">Metal</span> tradeoffs.</h2>\n<table class=\"tradeoffs-table\" aria-label=\"PlanetScale Metal versus Aurora persistent storage tradeoffs\">\n <colgroup><col class=\"tradeoff-dimension\"><col><col></colgroup>\n <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Tradeoff</th><th scope=\"col\">PlanetScale Metal<span>Local storage</span></th><th scope=\"col\">Aurora<span>Network storage</span></th></tr></thead>\n <tbody>\n  <tr><th scope=\"row\">Storage I/O</th><td><strong class=\"accent\">Local NVMe</strong><span>No separate storage network hop</span></td><td><strong>Network I/O</strong><span>Shared persistent volume</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th scope=\"row\">Storage growth</th><td><strong>Fixed drive capacity</strong><span>Reserve headroom; resize ahead</span></td><td><strong>Automatic volume growth</strong><span>Storage grows independently of compute</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th scope=\"row\">Resize effort</th><td><strong>Copies data to new drives</strong><span>Plan time for the data transfer</span></td><td><strong>Compute resizes separately</strong><span>Persistent data stays in the shared volume</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th scope=\"row\">I/O pricing</th><td><strong>No separate IOPS tier</strong><span>Pay for the selected drive capacity</span></td><td><strong>Standard: per-I/O charges</strong><span>I/O-Optimized: no read/write I/O charges</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th scope=\"row\">Decision</th><td><strong class=\"accent\">Is storage waiting material?</strong><span>Benchmark query tails and throughput</span></td><td><strong>How much growth flexibility?</strong><span>Weigh automatic growth and cache behavior</span></td></tr>\n </tbody>\n</table>",
    "hidden": true
  }
]
